  "honest_conclusion": "The 39-SNP bootstrap places K(1-K) in a tight interval, so the scale factor is 3.389 (95% CI ~3.385-3.421) and the forward ORs move <0.2%; K sampling error does not threaten the OR point estimates. However the +/-10% K perturbation moves the log-odds magnitude by ~10% while moving the OR by only ~0.4% -- the manuscript's habit of quoting OR-scale stability for robustness but log-odds magnitude for literature gaps is a reporting-scale switch that must be disclosed on both scales."
